## Dependencies and Risks

| Dependency | Risk | Mitigation |
|------------|------|------------|
| `express` | Low | Mature, well-understood. Already in AllowMe stack. |
| `x402-mcp` | Medium | Relatively new package. May have edge cases with mixed paid/free tools. Spike validated. Fallback: custom x402 middleware without x402-mcp wrapper. |
| `StreamableHTTPServerTransport` | Medium | MCP SDK transport. Session isolation confirmed in spike. Fallback: SSE transport if streaming issues arise. |
| `ALLOWANCE_AGENT_URL` env var | Low | Required for invite join messages and landing page. If unset, invite-member omits serverUrl and joinMessage — code-only invite still works. |
| Fitbit OAuth (`FITBIT_CLIENT_ID`, `FITBIT_CLIENT_SECRET`) | Medium | Requires AllowMe LLC Fitbit developer app registration. If Fitbit deprecates or rate-limits, health achievements fall back to manual self-report (`source: "self-report"`). |
| Fitbit token storage encryption | Low | AES-256-GCM keyed from existing `OWS_PASSPHRASE`. No new secrets. |
| Claude custom connectors (free plan, 1 connector) | Low | Free users get exactly 1 custom connector. AllowanceAgent uses it. If user already has a connector, they need Pro ($20/mo) or must remove the existing one. |
| Landing page hosting (Vercel) | Low | Static HTML, zero dependencies. Could also host on GitHub Pages or Netlify. |
| Child-scoped middleware | Low | Single enforcement point. Well-tested. |
| Passphrase env var | Low | Simple refactor. Env vars are standard for secrets. |
| `allowance-policy.py` ERC-20 decode fix | Medium | Calldata parsing is fragile. Defense-in-depth: app layer already tracks recipients. Policy is secondary check. |

## Fallback Approaches

- **HTTP transport fails:** Ship Learner role + source field + bug fixes on stdio. Defer x402, Fitbit OAuth, and landing page. Child connects by sharing parent's machine.
- **x402-mcp incompatible:** Build custom x402 middleware: intercept HTTP requests, check for payment header, verify via facilitator, forward to MCP handler.
- **Claude connector flow changes:** If Anthropic changes the Settings → Connectors UI, update landing page screenshots. The MCP server URL itself is stable.
- **Fitbit OAuth registration denied or rate-limited:** Health achievements fall back to manual self-report and parent attestation. AllowanceAgent works fully without Fitbit — it's an enhancement, not a dependency.
- **Fitbit token refresh fails:** Log error, mark token as invalid, tool returns "Fitbit connection expired — ask your parent to reconnect." One-tap reconnect via `/fitbit/connect`.
- **Child-scoping breaks existing tests:** Add childName as optional (default: null = all children). Existing tests pass unchanged.
- **Passphrase env var breaks CI:** Set `OWS_PASSPHRASE=test` in test env. Dry-run mode doesn't need real passphrase.
- **Free plan connector limit blocks families:** Document workaround in onboarding page. If user already has a connector, they can remove it or upgrade to Pro.

